pulse-volumeicon is a small system tray icon to control the sound volume.
Scroll over the icon to change the volume, middle click to toggle mute,
and left click for a menu.

It changes the volume through pactl, so it works with PulseAudio 15 or
newer and with PipeWire. The icon uses libayatana-appindicator, which
shows it in StatusNotifierItem trays (KDE Plasma, Xfce) and falls back
to an XEmbed icon in older trays.

Volume change notifications need a running notification daemon.
